/***********************************************************************************************************************
da4_gethandlersourcepage.probesql -- dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage (script 503).

Run: sqlcmd -S localhost -E -C -I -d RCRAInfo -y 0 -i "C:\~MDE-55TT2J4\RCRAInfo\build\tmp\da4_gethandlersourcepage.probesql"
-I is REQUIRED. dbo.HandlerSource carries a filtered unique index (UX_dbo_HandlerSource_Natural), and any write to a
table with one needs SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON or the insert fails with error 1934 naming indexed views.

CONVENTIONS THIS FILE FOLLOWS, ALL OF THEM LOAD-BEARING:

  * Every fixture row uses an MDPROBE0503% HandlerId, so the reset and the cleanup can find them without touching a
    real handler.
  * SOFT DELETE ONLY. There is no hard delete anywhere in this database, so cleanup sets IsDeleted = 1 and the fixture
    rows stay. The reset at the top retires anything a previous run left visible, which is what makes this file
    re-runnable.
  * REFUSALS use plain EXEC and successes use INSERT ... EXEC. That is not stylistic: INSERT ... EXEC opens a
    transaction, and a procedure that throws inside one leaves the transaction doomed (error 3930), so the CATCH cannot
    write its log row and the [R15] assertions below would measure nothing. See section A2.
  * INSERT ... EXEC IS ITSELF AN ASSERTION. #Page names all 22 columns in order, so a change to the projection's
    column list, order, or types fails the insert rather than passing silently. It also succeeds on an EMPTY result set
    and fails on a MISSING one, which a row count cannot tell apart.
  * ORDER is asserted with STRING_AGG over Ordinal, compared against a hand-computed expected string. The expectations
    are derived from the fixture by hand rather than by re-running the procedure's own predicate, so a wrong answer
    cannot agree with itself.

WHAT THE FIXTURE IS. Six VISIBLE rows and three that must never appear:

  #  HandlerId      Src Seq  HandlerName        Received    SrcUpdated  City        Gen  SortOrder
  1  MDPROBE05031   A   1    ZEBRA WORKS        2024-01-15  2026-01-10  Baltimore   1    30
  2  MDPROBE05032   B   1    ALPHA CHEMICAL     2024-03-20  2026-02-15  Annapolis   2    20
  3  MDPROBE05033   C   1    MIDLAND PLATING    2023-11-05  2026-03-01  Rockville   1    10
  4  MDPROBE05034   A   1    ALPHA CHEMICAL     2024-03-20  2026-04-12  Baltimore   3    30
  5  MDPROBE05035   D   1    NULLSORT CO        2025-06-01  2026-05-20  Frederick   1    NULL
  6  MDPROBE05036   B   2    BETA RECYCLING     2025-08-14  2026-06-30  Salisbury   2    20
  7  MDPROBE05037   A   1    HIDDEN SOFTDELETE      -- IsDeleted = 1
  8  MDPROBE05038   A   1    HIDDEN NOTCURRENT      -- CurrentRecord = 0
  9  MDPROBE05039   A   1    HIDDEN NULLCURRENT     -- CurrentRecord = NULL

Rows 2 and 4 share a HandlerName AND a ReceivedDate, which is what makes the tiebreaker assertions mean something.
Row 5 carries a NULL SourceTypeSortOrder, which is the case the SourceType sort has to order deterministically.
Rows 7 to 9 are the three separate ways dbo.vwHandlerSource excludes a row, and each is asserted separately -- 8 and 9
in particular, because `CurrentRecord = 1` excludes NULL and that is easy to get wrong when reading the view.

ActivityLocation is 'MD' on every row. No fixture row carries an out-of-state activityLocation: MDE's decision is that
out-of-state values appear on contacts and mailing addresses and never on activityLocation itself, so the negative test
below asks for 'VA' and expects nothing rather than inserting a 'VA' row.

dbo.HandlerSource holds 50 rows on this workstation, ALL soft-deleted, so dbo.vwHandlerSource exposes none of them and
the unfiltered totals asserted below are exactly the fixture's six. Section B cross-checks that against the view rather
than trusting the constant.
***********************************************************************************************************************/

SET NOCOUNT ON;
SET XACT_ABORT OFF;   -- the refusal sections need the batch to continue after a caught error
GO

PRINT N'=== da4_gethandlersourcepage: dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage ===';
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reset. Retire anything a previous run left visible. Soft delete only.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE dbo.HandlerSource
   SET IsDeleted             = 1
     , auditDeletedBy        = ORIGINAL_LOGIN ()
     , auditDeletedDateUtc   = SYSUTCDATETIME ()
     , auditModifiedBy       = ORIGINAL_LOGIN ()
     , auditModifiedDateUtc  = SYSUTCDATETIME ()
 WHERE HandlerId LIKE N'MDPROBE0503%'
   AND IsDeleted = 0;
PRINT CONCAT (N'reset: retired ', @@ROWCOUNT, N' leftover fixture row(s).');
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixture.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSERT INTO dbo.HandlerSource
    (HandlerId, ActivityLocation, SourceType, Sequence, CurrentRecord, IsDeleted
   , SourceTypeDescription, SourceTypeSortOrder, HandlerName, ReceivedDate, SrcUpdatedDate
   , SiteLocationAddress1, SiteLocationCity, SiteLocationStateCode, SiteLocationZip
   , SiteLocationCountyDescription, WasteFederalGeneratorCategoryCode
   , WasteFederalGeneratorCategoryDescription, WasteTsd, WasteTransporter, WasteRecyclerActivity)
VALUES
  (N'MDPROBE05031', N'MD', N'A', 1, 1, 0, N'Notification',   30, N'ZEBRA WORKS',        '2024-01-15', '2026-01-10', N'1 Zebra St',   N'Baltimore', N'MD', N'21201', N'Baltimore City',    N'1', N'LQG',  1, 0, 0)
, (N'MDPROBE05032', N'MD', N'B', 1, 1, 0, N'Part A',         20, N'ALPHA CHEMICAL',     '2024-03-20', '2026-02-15', N'2 Alpha Rd',   N'Annapolis', N'MD', N'21401', N'Anne Arundel',      N'2', N'SQG',  0, 1, 0)
, (N'MDPROBE05033', N'MD', N'C', 1, 1, 0, N'Permit',         10, N'MIDLAND PLATING',    '2023-11-05', '2026-03-01', N'3 Midland Ave',N'Rockville', N'MD', N'20850', N'Montgomery',        N'1', N'LQG',  0, 0, 1)
, (N'MDPROBE05034', N'MD', N'A', 1, 1, 0, N'Notification',   30, N'ALPHA CHEMICAL',     '2024-03-20', '2026-04-12', N'4 Alpha Rd',   N'Baltimore', N'MD', N'21202', N'Baltimore City',    N'3', N'VSQG', 0, 0, 0)
, (N'MDPROBE05035', N'MD', N'D', 1, 1, 0, NULL,            NULL, N'NULLSORT CO',        '2025-06-01', '2026-05-20', N'5 Null Way',   N'Frederick', N'MD', N'21701', N'Frederick',         N'1', N'LQG',  0, 0, 0)
, (N'MDPROBE05036', N'MD', N'B', 2, 1, 0, N'Part A',         20, N'BETA RECYCLING',     '2025-08-14', '2026-06-30', N'6 Beta Blvd',  N'Salisbury', N'MD', N'21801', N'Wicomico',          N'2', N'SQG',  0, 0, 1)
  -- The three exclusions. 7 is soft-deleted, 8 is a superseded version, 9 was never stamped by the reconcile pass.
, (N'MDPROBE05037', N'MD', N'A', 1,    1, 1, N'Notification', 30, N'HIDDEN SOFTDELETE',  '2024-01-15', '2026-01-10', N'7 Gone St',    N'Baltimore', N'MD', N'21201', N'Baltimore City',   N'1', N'LQG',  0, 0, 0)
, (N'MDPROBE05038', N'MD', N'A', 1,    0, 0, N'Notification', 30, N'HIDDEN NOTCURRENT', '2024-01-15', '2026-01-10', N'8 Old St',     N'Baltimore', N'MD', N'21201', N'Baltimore City',   N'1', N'LQG',  0, 0, 0)
, (N'MDPROBE05039', N'MD', N'A', 1, NULL, 0, N'Notification', 30, N'HIDDEN NULLCURRENT','2024-01-15', '2026-01-10', N'9 Unstamped St',N'Baltimore',N'MD', N'21201', N'Baltimore City',   N'1', N'LQG',  0, 0, 0);
PRINT CONCAT (N'fixture: inserted ', @@ROWCOUNT, N' row(s).');
GO

-- The shape assertion. All 22 columns, in the procedure's order.
CREATE TABLE #Page
(
    Ordinal                                  INT            NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY
  , HandlerSourceId                          INT            NOT NULL
  , HandlerId                                NVARCHAR (12)  NOT NULL
  , ActivityLocation                         NVARCHAR (2)   NOT NULL
  , SourceType                               NVARCHAR (1)   NOT NULL
  , SourceTypeDescription                    NVARCHAR (255) NULL
  , Sequence                                 INT            NOT NULL
  , ReceivedDate                             DATE           NULL
  , HandlerName                              NVARCHAR (80)  NULL
  , SiteLocationAddress1                     NVARCHAR (50)  NULL
  , SiteLocationCity                         NVARCHAR (25)  NULL
  , SiteLocationStateCode                    NVARCHAR (2)   NULL
  , SiteLocationZip                          NVARCHAR (14)  NULL
  , SiteLocationCountyDescription            NVARCHAR (255) NULL
  , WasteFederalGeneratorCategoryCode        NVARCHAR (1)   NULL
  , WasteFederalGeneratorCategoryDescription NVARCHAR (255) NULL
  , WasteTsd                                 BIT            NULL
  , WasteTransporter                         BIT            NULL
  , WasteRecyclerActivity                    BIT            NULL
  , SrcUpdatedDate                           DATE           NULL
  , auditModifiedDateUtc                     DATETIME2      NOT NULL
  , TotalRows                                INT            NOT NULL
);
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- A. Refusals. Plain EXEC, never INSERT ... EXEC -- see the header.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- A. refusals ---';
GO
BEGIN TRY
    EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'HandlerID_typo';
    PRINT N'FAIL A1: a @SortBy outside the whitelist returned rows instead of throwing.';
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    IF ERROR_MESSAGE () LIKE N'%is not a sortable column of this grid%'
       AND ERROR_MESSAGE () LIKE N'%rejected rather than defaulted%'
        PRINT N'PASS A1: an unrecognised @SortBy is refused, and the message says why it is not defaulted.';
    ELSE
        PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A1: wrong message -- ', ERROR_MESSAGE ());
END CATCH;
GO
BEGIN TRY
    EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = NULL;
    PRINT N'FAIL A2: @SortBy = NULL returned rows instead of throwing.';
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    IF ERROR_MESSAGE () LIKE N'%@SortBy = NULL is not a sortable column%'
        PRINT N'PASS A2: @SortBy = NULL is refused and the message renders NULL as NULL, not as an empty string.';
    ELSE
        PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A2: wrong message -- ', ERROR_MESSAGE ());
END CATCH;
GO
-- Case-insensitivity is the other half of the whitelist: a JavaScript grid sends lower camel case.
BEGIN TRY
    DECLARE @n INT;
    CREATE TABLE #ci (a INT, b INT, c NVARCHAR (12), d NVARCHAR (2), e NVARCHAR (1), f NVARCHAR (255)
                    , g INT, h DATE, i NVARCHAR (80), j NVARCHAR (50), k NVARCHAR (25), l NVARCHAR (2)
                    , m NVARCHAR (14), n NVARCHAR (255), o NVARCHAR (1), p NVARCHAR (255), q BIT, r BIT
                    , s BIT, t DATE, u DATETIME2, v INT);
    INSERT INTO #ci EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'handlerName';
    SELECT @n = COUNT (*) FROM #ci;
    IF @n = 6 PRINT N'PASS A3: @SortBy is matched case-insensitively, so ''handlerName'' is accepted.';
    ELSE      PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A3: expected 6 rows, got ', @n);
    DROP TABLE #ci;
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A3: ''handlerName'' was refused -- ', ERROR_MESSAGE ());
END CATCH;
GO
BEGIN TRY
    EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ReceivedFromDate = '2025-01-01', @ReceivedToDate = '2024-01-01';
    PRINT N'FAIL A4: an inverted received-date range returned rows instead of throwing.';
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    IF ERROR_MESSAGE () LIKE N'%is later than @ReceivedToDate%'
       AND ERROR_MESSAGE () LIKE N'%cannot match a row for any data%'
        PRINT N'PASS A4: an inverted received-date range is refused as arithmetic, not returned as an empty page.';
    ELSE
        PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A4: wrong message -- ', ERROR_MESSAGE ());
END CATCH;
GO
BEGIN TRY
    EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SrcUpdatedFromDate = '2026-12-31', @SrcUpdatedToDate = '2026-01-01';
    PRINT N'FAIL A5: an inverted SrcUpdated range returned rows instead of throwing.';
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    IF ERROR_MESSAGE () LIKE N'%is later than @SrcUpdatedToDate%'
        PRINT N'PASS A5: an inverted SrcUpdated range is refused.';
    ELSE
        PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A5: wrong message -- ', ERROR_MESSAGE ());
END CATCH;
GO
-- An EQUAL pair is a one-day window and must NOT be refused. The boundary matters: `>` not `>=`.
BEGIN TRY
    DECLARE @n INT;
    CREATE TABLE #eq (a INT, b INT, c NVARCHAR (12), d NVARCHAR (2), e NVARCHAR (1), f NVARCHAR (255)
                    , g INT, h DATE, i NVARCHAR (80), j NVARCHAR (50), k NVARCHAR (25), l NVARCHAR (2)
                    , m NVARCHAR (14), n NVARCHAR (255), o NVARCHAR (1), p NVARCHAR (255), q BIT, r BIT
                    , s BIT, t DATE, u DATETIME2, v INT);
    INSERT INTO #eq EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ReceivedFromDate = '2024-03-20', @ReceivedToDate = '2024-03-20';
    SELECT @n = COUNT (*) FROM #eq;
    IF @n = 2 PRINT N'PASS A6: From = To is a one-day window and returns its 2 rows, not a refusal.';
    ELSE      PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A6: expected 2 rows for the single-day window, got ', @n);
    DROP TABLE #eq;
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A6: From = To was refused -- ', ERROR_MESSAGE ());
END CATCH;
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- A2. [R15]. Every refusal above must have left an ORPHAN row in logs.ExecutionLog: this procedure writes no start
--     row, so the CATCH inserts rather than updates. That is the whole point of the instrumentation -- a read that
--     fails and records nothing is the defect this project exists to prevent.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- A2. the error rows the refusals had to write ---';
GO
DECLARE @Orphans INT, @Bad INT, @NoElapsed INT;

SELECT @Orphans = COUNT (*)
  FROM logs.ExecutionLog
 WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
   AND Successful    = 0
   AND StartDateUtc >= DATEADD (MINUTE, -10, SYSUTCDATETIME ());

IF @Orphans >= 4 PRINT CONCAT (N'PASS A2.1: the refusals recorded themselves -- ', @Orphans, N' error row(s).');
ELSE             PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A2.1: expected at least 4 error rows, found ', @Orphans);

-- The orphan signature: Successful = 0, EndDateUtc set, ElapsedMilliseconds NULL. The NULL is what identifies an
-- orphan, so a value there would make one indistinguishable from a closed-out row.
SELECT @Bad = COUNT (*)
  FROM logs.ExecutionLog
 WHERE ProcedureName        = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
   AND Successful           = 0
   AND StartDateUtc        >= DATEADD (MINUTE, -10, SYSUTCDATETIME ())
   AND ElapsedMilliseconds IS NOT NULL;
IF @Bad = 0 PRINT N'PASS A2.2: every error row is a true orphan -- ElapsedMilliseconds is NULL, which is its signature.';
ELSE        PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A2.2: ', @Bad, N' error row(s) carry an ElapsedMilliseconds they cannot have earned.');

-- ...so the duration has to be recoverable from somewhere, and the CATCH puts it in ContextMessage.
SELECT @NoElapsed = COUNT (*)
  FROM logs.ExecutionLog
 WHERE ProcedureName   = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
   AND Successful      = 0
   AND StartDateUtc   >= DATEADD (MINUTE, -10, SYSUTCDATETIME ())
   AND COALESCE (ContextMessage, N'') NOT LIKE N'%ElapsedMs=%';
IF @NoElapsed = 0 PRINT N'PASS A2.3: every error row carries ElapsedMs= in ContextMessage, so the duration is not lost.';
ELSE              PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A2.3: ', @NoElapsed, N' error row(s) have no ElapsedMs= in ContextMessage.');

-- KeyParameters must record what the CALLER sent, so a bad @SortBy is visible in it verbatim.
IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM logs.ExecutionLog
            WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
              AND Successful    = 0
              AND KeyParameters LIKE N'%SortBy=HandlerID_typo%')
    PRINT N'PASS A2.4: KeyParameters records the rejected @SortBy as the caller sent it.';
ELSE
    PRINT N'FAIL A2.4: no error row records the rejected @SortBy in KeyParameters.';

-- A NULL argument must log as (any)/(null), never as an empty string -- CONCAT renders NULL as '', which would make
-- the message read as truncated rather than as absent.
IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM logs.ExecutionLog
            WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
              AND Successful    = 0
              AND KeyParameters LIKE N'%HandlerId=(any)%')
    PRINT N'PASS A2.5: omitted filters log as (any) rather than as an empty string.';
ELSE
    PRINT N'FAIL A2.5: an omitted filter did not log as (any).';
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- A3. G37. A CATCH inside a transaction the CALLER owns cannot write its log row at all: XACT_ABORT ON dooms the
--     transaction (error 3930) and the insert is impossible by any means. This is measured rather than assumed, and
--     the assertion is written to SHOUT if the answer ever changes.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- A3. G37, the boundary this procedure cannot cross ---';
GO
DECLARE @Before INT, @After INT, @State INT;
SELECT @Before = COUNT (*) FROM logs.ExecutionLog WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]';

BEGIN TRANSACTION;   -- the CALLER's transaction, which this procedure must never roll back
BEGIN TRY
    EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'nope';
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    SET @State = XACT_STATE ();
END CATCH;
IF XACT_STATE () <> 0 ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;

SELECT @After = COUNT (*) FROM logs.ExecutionLog WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]';

IF @State = -1 AND @After = @Before
    PRINT CONCAT (N'PASS A3.1: inside a caller''s transaction XACT_STATE = ', @State
                , N' and 0 rows were recorded. That is G37, still open and still documented.');
ELSE IF @After > @Before
    PRINT CONCAT (N'CHANGED A3.1: something now CAN record here (', @After - @Before
                , N' row(s), XACT_STATE = ', @State, N'). G37 may be resolved -- update the docs.');
ELSE
    PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL A3.1: unexpected state ', COALESCE (CAST (@State AS NVARCHAR (11)), N'(null)'));
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- B. The default page, and TotalRows cross-checked against the view rather than against a constant.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- B. the default page ---';
GO
DELETE FROM #Page;
INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage;   -- succeeds only if all 22 columns still match, in order
GO
DECLARE @Rows INT, @Total INT, @Independent INT, @Order NVARCHAR (400);
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = MAX (TotalRows) FROM #Page;
SELECT @Independent = COUNT (*) FROM dbo.vwHandlerSource;

IF @Rows = 6 PRINT N'PASS B1: the default call returns the fixture''s 6 visible rows.';
ELSE         PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL B1: expected 6 rows, got ', @Rows);

IF @Total = @Independent
    PRINT CONCAT (N'PASS B2: TotalRows (', @Total, N') equals an independent COUNT (*) over dbo.vwHandlerSource.');
ELSE
    PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL B2: TotalRows = ', @Total, N' but the view holds ', @Independent, N' visible row(s).');

IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM #Page GROUP BY TotalRows HAVING COUNT (*) = 6)
    PRINT N'PASS B3: TotalRows is the same on every row, which is what a scalar rather than a window function means.';
ELSE
    PRINT N'FAIL B3: TotalRows differs between rows on one page.';

-- Ordinal must be 1..n with no gaps, because the grid's "showing 51-75 of 340" caption reads it directly.
IF (SELECT COUNT (*) FROM #Page WHERE Ordinal BETWEEN 1 AND 6) = 6 AND (SELECT MIN (Ordinal) FROM #Page) = 1
    PRINT N'PASS B4: Ordinal is 1..6 with no gaps.';
ELSE
    PRINT N'FAIL B4: Ordinal is not a gapless 1..6.';

SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05034,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05036'
    PRINT N'PASS B5: the default sort is HandlerId ascending.';
ELSE
    PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL B5: default order was ', @Order);
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- C. The projection. 22 named columns in order, and NO contact PII.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- C. the projection ---';
GO
DECLARE @Actual NVARCHAR (MAX), @Expected NVARCHAR (MAX), @Leaked NVARCHAR (400);

SELECT @Actual = STRING_AGG (r.name, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY r.column_ordinal)
  FROM sys.dm_exec_describe_first_result_set (N'EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage', NULL, 0) AS r;

SET @Expected = N'Ordinal,HandlerSourceId,HandlerId,ActivityLocation,SourceType,SourceTypeDescription,Sequence,'
              + N'ReceivedDate,HandlerName,SiteLocationAddress1,SiteLocationCity,SiteLocationStateCode,'
              + N'SiteLocationZip,SiteLocationCountyDescription,WasteFederalGeneratorCategoryCode,'
              + N'WasteFederalGeneratorCategoryDescription,WasteTsd,WasteTransporter,WasteRecyclerActivity,'
              + N'SrcUpdatedDate,auditModifiedDateUtc,TotalRows';

IF @Actual = @Expected PRINT N'PASS C1: the projection is exactly the 22 documented columns, in order.';
ELSE                   PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL C1: the projection changed. Got: ', @Actual);

-- The PII exclusion, asserted by NAME rather than by counting. Contact columns, SrcUpdatedBy (an EPA user) and
-- IsDeleted (a constant 0 through this view) must all be absent.
SELECT @Leaked = STRING_AGG (r.name, N',')
  FROM sys.dm_exec_describe_first_result_set (N'EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage', NULL, 0) AS r
 WHERE r.name LIKE N'Contact%'
    OR r.name LIKE N'%ContactEmail%'
    OR r.name LIKE N'%ContactPhone%'
    OR r.name IN (N'SrcUpdatedBy', N'SrcCreatedBy', N'IsDeleted', N'auditDeletedBy', N'auditDeletedDateUtc');

IF @Leaked IS NULL
    PRINT N'PASS C2: no contact PII, no EPA user name, and no constant IsDeleted in the grid projection.';
ELSE
    PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL C2: the grid now returns ', @Leaked);
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- D. Every filter, TotalRows against a hand-computed expectation. This is the check the header promises: the WHERE
--    clause is written TWICE in 503, and a filter added to one copy and not the other makes TotalRows a count of a
--    different set than the page. Both are asserted on every row here.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- D. the filters, and the two copies of the WHERE clause agreeing ---';
GO
DECLARE @Label NVARCHAR (60), @Expect INT, @Rows INT, @Total INT;

-- D1 HandlerId
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @HandlerId = N'MDPROBE05031';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 1 AND @Total = 1 PRINT N'PASS D1: @HandlerId matches its one row and TotalRows agrees.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D1: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 1/1');

-- D2 ActivityLocation, both directions
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ActivityLocation = N'MD';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 6 AND @Total = 6 PRINT N'PASS D2: @ActivityLocation = MD matches all 6.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D2: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 6/6');

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ActivityLocation = N'VA';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 0 PRINT N'PASS D3: an unmatched @ActivityLocation returns an empty page rather than throwing -- it is not a closed set.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D3: expected 0 rows for VA, got ', @Rows);

-- D4 SourceType. Also not a closed set: an unknown code must return nothing, not refuse.
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SourceType = N'A';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 2 AND @Total = 2 PRINT N'PASS D4: @SourceType = A matches its 2 rows.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D4: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 2/2');

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SourceType = N'Z';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 0 PRINT N'PASS D5: an unknown @SourceType returns nothing rather than refusing -- dbo.HandlerSource closes no set.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D5: expected 0 rows for SourceType Z, got ', @Rows);

-- D6 generator category
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @FederalGeneratorCategory = N'1';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 3 AND @Total = 3 PRINT N'PASS D6: @FederalGeneratorCategory = 1 matches its 3 rows.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D6: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 3/3');

-- D7/D8 received-date bounds, each on its own, so an omitted bound is proved not to filter
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ReceivedFromDate = '2024-01-01';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 5 AND @Total = 5 PRINT N'PASS D7: @ReceivedFromDate alone is inclusive and matches 5.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D7: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 5/5');

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ReceivedToDate = '2024-03-20';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 4 AND @Total = 4 PRINT N'PASS D8: @ReceivedToDate alone is inclusive and matches 4.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D8: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 4/4');

-- D9 both bounds together
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @ReceivedFromDate = '2024-01-01', @ReceivedToDate = '2024-12-31';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 3 AND @Total = 3 PRINT N'PASS D9: the received-date window matches its 3 rows.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D9: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 3/3');

-- D10/D11 SrcUpdated bounds
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SrcUpdatedFromDate = '2026-03-01';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 4 AND @Total = 4 PRINT N'PASS D10: @SrcUpdatedFromDate matches its 4 rows.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D10: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 4/4');

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SrcUpdatedToDate = '2026-02-15';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 2 AND @Total = 2 PRINT N'PASS D11: @SrcUpdatedToDate matches its 2 rows.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D11: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 2/2');

-- D12 two different filters together, which is where a missing AND in one copy would show
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SourceType = N'A', @FederalGeneratorCategory = N'1';
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 1 AND @Total = 1 PRINT N'PASS D12: two filters combine, and both copies of the WHERE clause agree.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL D12: rows=', @Rows, N' total=', @Total, N' expected 1/1');
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- E. Sorting. Order asserted as a string, against expectations computed by hand from the fixture table in the header.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- E. sorting, including the tiebreaker and the SourceType special case ---';
GO
DECLARE @Order NVARCHAR (400);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'HandlerName', @SortDescending = 0;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05034,MDPROBE05036,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05031'
    PRINT N'PASS E1: HandlerName ascending, with the two ALPHA CHEMICAL rows broken by HandlerSourceId ascending.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL E1: ', @Order);

-- The tiebreaker does NOT flip with @SortDescending -- it only has to be deterministic. So the two ALPHA rows stay in
-- 32,34 order even though everything around them reverses.
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'HandlerName', @SortDescending = 1;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05036,MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05034'
    PRINT N'PASS E2: HandlerName descending reverses, and the tiebreaker stays ASCENDING as the header claims.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL E2: ', @Order);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'ReceivedDate', @SortDescending = 0;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05034,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05036'
    PRINT N'PASS E3: ReceivedDate ascending, with the shared 2024-03-20 broken by the surrogate key.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL E3: ', @Order);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'SrcUpdatedDate', @SortDescending = 1;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05036,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05034,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05031'
    PRINT N'PASS E4: SrcUpdatedDate descending -- the "what did EPA change lately" sort.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL E4: ', @Order);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'SiteLocationCity', @SortDescending = 0;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05034,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05036'
    PRINT N'PASS E5: SiteLocationCity ascending, with the two Baltimore rows broken by the surrogate key.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL E5: ', @Order);

-- The one column where the value SORTED is not the value SHOWN. SourceTypeSortOrder is 10,20,20,30,30,NULL, and NULL
-- sorts first ascending -- so the row with no lookup entry leads, which is deliberate and is what this asserts.
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @SortBy = N'SourceType', @SortDescending = 0;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05036,MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05034'
    PRINT N'PASS E6: SourceType sorts by SourceTypeSortOrder (NULL first), then the code, then the surrogate key.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL E6: ', @Order);
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- F. Paging. Pages must partition the ordered set exactly: no row on two pages, no row on none.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- F. paging ---';
GO
CREATE TABLE #All (Src NVARCHAR (10), Ordinal INT, HandlerId NVARCHAR (12), TotalRows INT);
GO
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Skip = 0, @Take = 2;
INSERT INTO #All SELECT N'p1', Ordinal, HandlerId, TotalRows FROM #Page;
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Skip = 2, @Take = 2;
INSERT INTO #All SELECT N'p2', Ordinal, HandlerId, TotalRows FROM #Page;
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Skip = 4, @Take = 2;
INSERT INTO #All SELECT N'p3', Ordinal, HandlerId, TotalRows FROM #Page;
GO
DECLARE @Order NVARCHAR (400), @Rows INT, @Distinct INT, @Totals INT;
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*), @Distinct = COUNT (DISTINCT HandlerId), @Totals = COUNT (DISTINCT TotalRows) FROM #All;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #All;

IF @Rows = 6 AND @Distinct = 6
    PRINT N'PASS F1: three pages of 2 partition the set -- 6 rows, 6 distinct, nothing repeated and nothing skipped.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL F1: rows=', @Rows, N' distinct=', @Distinct);

IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05032,MDPROBE05033,MDPROBE05034,MDPROBE05035,MDPROBE05036'
    PRINT N'PASS F2: Ordinal is absolute across pages, so concatenating them reproduces the full order.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL F2: ', @Order);

IF @Totals = 1 PRINT N'PASS F3: TotalRows is the filtered total, not the page size -- identical on all three pages.';
ELSE           PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL F3: TotalRows varied across pages (', @Totals, N' distinct values).');

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Skip = 100;
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 0 PRINT N'PASS F4: a page past the end is empty -- and TotalRows is unreadable from it, as the header warns.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL F4: expected 0 rows past the end, got ', @Rows);
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- G. Clamping. The procedure is the boundary, so the clamp has to hold no matter what the caller sends.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- G. clamping ---';
GO
DECLARE @Rows INT, @Order NVARCHAR (400);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Take = 100000;
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 6 PRINT N'PASS G1: @Take = 100000 is clamped to 500 and returns the 6 rows that exist, not an error.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL G1: got ', @Rows);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Take = 0;
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 1 PRINT N'PASS G2: @Take = 0 is floored to 1 -- a grid asking for nothing gets one row, not zero.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL G2: expected 1 row, got ', @Rows);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Take = NULL;
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 6 PRINT N'PASS G3: @Take = NULL means the default 50, not the floor of 1.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL G3: expected 6 rows, got ', @Rows);

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Skip = -5, @Take = 2;
SELECT @Order = STRING_AGG (HandlerId, N',') WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY Ordinal) FROM #Page;
IF @Order = N'MDPROBE05031,MDPROBE05032'
    PRINT N'PASS G4: a negative @Skip is floored to 0 rather than failing OFFSET with an error the grid cannot act on.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL G4: ', @Order);

-- The @Skip ceiling is not cosmetic: the paging predicate is `Ordinal <= @Skip + @Take`, and a @Skip near the INT
-- maximum would overflow that sum and fail the call with an arithmetic error.
DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Skip = 2147483647, @Take = 50;
SELECT @Rows = COUNT (*) FROM #Page;
IF @Rows = 0 PRINT N'PASS G5: @Skip at the INT maximum returns an empty page instead of overflowing @Skip + @Take.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL G5: expected 0 rows, got ', @Rows);
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- H. The three ways dbo.vwHandlerSource excludes a row. Asserted separately, because they fail separately.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- H. what must never appear ---';
GO
DECLARE @Rows INT, @Total INT;

DELETE FROM #Page; INSERT INTO #Page EXEC dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage @Take = 500;
SELECT @Total = COALESCE (MAX (TotalRows), 0) FROM #Page;

IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM #Page WHERE HandlerId = N'MDPROBE05037')
    PRINT N'PASS H1: the soft-deleted row is invisible, and there is no @IncludeDeleted to make it visible.';
ELSE PRINT N'FAIL H1: a soft-deleted row reached the grid.';

IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM #Page WHERE HandlerId = N'MDPROBE05038')
    PRINT N'PASS H2: a superseded version (CurrentRecord = 0) is invisible -- history is 504''s question.';
ELSE PRINT N'FAIL H2: a non-current row reached the grid.';

IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM #Page WHERE HandlerId = N'MDPROBE05039')
    PRINT N'PASS H3: CurrentRecord = NULL is invisible too, because `= 1` excludes NULL. That is the reconcile-pass gap the header names.';
ELSE PRINT N'FAIL H3: a NULL-CurrentRecord row reached the grid.';

IF @Total = 6 PRINT N'PASS H4: TotalRows counts 6, not 9 -- the exclusions are applied to the COUNT as well as to the page.';
ELSE PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL H4: TotalRows = ', @Total, N', expected 6.');
GO

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- I. Nothing credential-shaped in what this procedure logs.
-- =====================================================================================================================
PRINT N'';
PRINT N'--- I. what got logged ---';
GO
DECLARE @Bad INT, @Sample NVARCHAR (MAX);
-- The OR group is parenthesised deliberately. Without the brackets AND binds tighter, every OR branch loses the
-- ProcedureName restriction, and the check silently becomes "does ANY procedure in logs.ExecutionLog log something
-- credential-shaped" -- a different and much noisier question than the one this section asks.
SELECT @Bad = COUNT (*)
  FROM logs.ExecutionLog
 WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
   AND (   (COALESCE (KeyParameters, N'') + COALESCE (ContextMessage, N'') + COALESCE (Comments, N''))
               LIKE N'%[?&]%'   -- a query string would arrive carrying one of these
        OR COALESCE (KeyParameters, N'') LIKE N'%api%'
        OR COALESCE (KeyParameters, N'') LIKE N'%key%'
        OR COALESCE (KeyParameters, N'') LIKE N'%token%'
        OR COALESCE (KeyParameters, N'') LIKE N'%bearer%'
        OR COALESCE (KeyParameters, N'') LIKE N'%password%');
IF @Bad = 0 PRINT N'PASS I1: nothing credential-shaped or query-string-shaped in KeyParameters, ContextMessage or Comments.';
ELSE        PRINT CONCAT (N'FAIL I1: ', @Bad, N' logged row(s) match a credential-shaped pattern.');

SELECT TOP (1) @Sample = KeyParameters
  FROM logs.ExecutionLog
 WHERE ProcedureName = N'[dbo].[uspGetHandlerSourcePage]'
 ORDER BY ExecutionLogId DESC;
PRINT CONCAT (N'       sample KeyParameters: ', COALESCE (@Sample, N'(none)'));
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cleanup. Soft delete only -- the fixture rows stay in the table and the next run retires them again.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE dbo.HandlerSource
   SET IsDeleted             = 1
     , auditDeletedBy        = ORIGINAL_LOGIN ()
     , auditDeletedDateUtc   = SYSUTCDATETIME ()
     , auditModifiedBy       = ORIGINAL_LOGIN ()
     , auditModifiedDateUtc  = SYSUTCDATETIME ()
 WHERE HandlerId LIKE N'MDPROBE0503%'
   AND IsDeleted = 0;
PRINT CONCAT (N'cleanup: retired ', @@ROWCOUNT, N' fixture row(s).');
DROP TABLE #Page;
DROP TABLE #All;
GO

PRINT N'';
PRINT N'da4_gethandlersourcepage: done.';
GO
